      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T14:04:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I recall Rob mentioning that we don\u0027t handle color spaces yet. Do we currently do color transformations within graphite? All I see in the SkSl is:\n\n  16\t\thalf4 initialColor \u003d half4(0);\n  17\t\t// SolidColor\n  18\t\thalf4 outColor_0 \u003d sk_solid_shader(color_0);\n  19\t\t// FixedFunctionBlender\n  20\t\thalf4 outColor_1 \u003d outColor_0;\n  21\t\tsk_FragColor \u003d outColor_1;\n\nBut it\u0027s possible we are handling it on the CPU side and I am just missing it. Let me know. For now, I added a TODO in Device.cpp.",
      "revId": "145345982e7507f9e8b9386b25bd46b36b0c705d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
